For each word below, write ONE short sentence (12 to 22 words) that uses the word itself, spelled in full, in the sense given. Give it voice and mood: a question, someone speaking, a sigh, delight, a warning. No definitions; show the word in a moment of life. Answer as one JSON object mapping each WORD (as given, upper case) to its sentence. JSON only.

DOUBLE: a base hit on which the batter stops safely at second base.
DRAWER: a boxlike container in a piece of furniture.
EDITION: the form in which a text (especially a printed book) is published.
ELECTRON: an elementary particle with negative charge.
EMIT: expel (gases or odors).
ENTITY: that which is perceived or known or inferred to have its own distinct existence (living or nonliving).
